# ALLOWLIST. Everything at the repo root is excluded from the www deployment,
# then only the public marketing site is let back in. Anything not re-included
# below is not uploaded and not served.
#
# This used to be a denylist, and every internal file nobody had thought to
# list was public: CLAUDE.md, the whole app/ source tree (including
# migrations), automation/n8n/, scripts/ and .github/ all returned 200 on
# https://www.tradingsocial.io until 2026-09-18.
#
# Adding a new public file or folder at the root? Add a `!/<name>` line here,
# or it will 404 in production. Syntax is .gitignore's; see
# https://vercel.com/docs/deployments/vercel-ignore#allowlist
#
# app/ is its own Vercel project (app.tradingsocial.io, Root Directory `app`)
# and has its own app/.vercelignore, so nothing in this file applies to it.
/*

# Pages. Covers index, pricing, blog, blog-post, terms, privacy, disclaimer, 404.
!/*.html
!/compare
!/for

# Static files the pages load.
!/assets
!/consent.js
!/favicon.ico
!/robots.txt
!/sitemap.xml

# Fetched at runtime by blog.html and blog-post.html.
!/data

# Deployment config. Read by Vercel, not served.
!/vercel.json

# Internal notes inside otherwise-public folders.
/assets/**/*.md
